  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposal is therefore not a lawful development, and planning permission is required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;It appears to the local planning authority that the subject dwelling forms part of a development approved by planning permission WEST/112/02/OUT, dated 16/10/2002. Condition 12 of the planning permission restricts development within the curtilage of any dwellinghouse erected on the site that would otherwise be permitted by Clause 4 of Article 3&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Part 1, Classes A to E (inclusive) of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order with or without modification). It is, therefore, the opinion of the local planning authority that the proposed development cannot be carried out within the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015, as amended.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
